window.CHAPTERS = [{"num":1,"title":"A Strange Discovery","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"Camila leaned forward, her hands gripping the edge of her desk. The glowing computer screen in front of her showed a series of images from the Hubble (Hu-bull) Space "},{"t":"g","k":"telescope","v":"Telescope"},{"t":"t","v":". She blinked and looked again, her heart racing. Something was moving in the "},{"t":"g","k":"depths","v":"depths"},{"t":"t","v":" of space. It wasn't a planet or a star. It wasn't an asteroid or a comet. It was something new. Something "},{"t":"g","k":"massive","v":"massive"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She tapped a few keys, zooming in. The object was sleek and smooth, like a ship. But there wasn't just one. There were many. A "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" of enormous ships moving together through the "},{"t":"g","k":"cosmos","v":"cosmos"},{"t":"t","v":". They were heading toward Earth."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila grabbed her phone and dialed Zoe. \"Zoe, get to the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":". Now,\" she said, her voice barely above a whisper."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe — the sharpest "},{"t":"g","k":"physicist","v":"physicist"},{"t":"t","v":" Camila knew — arrived in minutes, already out of breath. She never walked when she could half-run. \"Okay, Cam. What's got you whispering?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila pointed at the screen. \"Ships. A "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" of them. They're traveling at "},{"t":"g","k":"half the speed of light","v":"half the speed of light"},{"t":"t","v":", and they're twenty light-years away.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe's jaw dropped. She started pacing — she always paced when her brain moved faster than her mouth. \""},{"t":"g","k":"half the speed of light","v":"Half the speed of light"},{"t":"t","v":". Twenty light-years. That means… they'll be here in three hundred years.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"One by one, the rest of the team arrived."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy came in carrying a tablet and a coffee. She was the best "},{"t":"g","k":"engineer","v":"engineer"},{"t":"t","v":" on the planet, and she didn't believe anything until she saw the numbers. She studied the "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":", frowning. \"If they're moving this fast, they have "},{"t":"g","k":"propulsion","v":"propulsion"},{"t":"t","v":" we can't even dream of. This is not a "},{"t":"g","k":"natural phenomenon","v":"natural phenomenon"},{"t":"t","v":". This is built.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava followed, her brow furrowed. Ava was a "},{"t":"g","k":"biologist","v":"biologist"},{"t":"t","v":", and she always asked the questions about living things first. \"Do we know if they're "},{"t":"g","k":"organic","v":"organic"},{"t":"t","v":"? Do they need oxygen? Water? Food?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya, an expert in deep-sea exploration, leaned against the wall. She was the bravest person Camila had ever met. \"How do we even talk to them? If they're this "},{"t":"g","k":"advanced","v":"advanced"},{"t":"t","v":", they might already know we're here.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle, a "},{"t":"g","k":"strategist","v":"strategist"},{"t":"t","v":", crossed her arms. She had the sharpest tongue of the group, and the quickest mind. \"The real question is: why are they coming?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila took a deep breath. \"We need to find a way to communicate with them.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The next few months were a blur of research and work. Camila and her team used Earth's largest radio telescopes to send signals into space. They tried different "},{"t":"g","k":"frequencies","v":"frequencies"},{"t":"t","v":". Different codes. Days turned into weeks. Then, one night, a reply came."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A strange, "},{"t":"g","k":"artificial","v":"artificial"},{"t":"t","v":" voice echoed through their speakers."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We are the Fortitude. Our home star is dying. We must find a new planet. We will arrive in three "},{"t":"g","k":"centuries","v":"centuries"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" went silent. The Fortitude were not coming as friends. They were not coming as "},{"t":"g","k":"invaders","v":"invaders"},{"t":"t","v":". They were coming because they had no choice. They needed a new home."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And that new home, Camila realized, might be Earth."}]]},{"num":2,"title":"The Doubters","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The news went public the next morning."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila had not wanted it to. She had wanted one more week to check the "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":", one more week to be sure. But the story leaked. Someone in the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" talked to a "},{"t":"g","k":"reporter","v":"reporter"},{"t":"t","v":". By sunrise, her face was on every screen in the world."}],[{"t":"g","k":"astronomer","v":"ASTRONOMER"},{"t":"t","v":" SPOTS "},{"t":"g","k":"alien","v":"ALIEN"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"FLEET"},{"t":"t","v":", the "},{"t":"g","k":"headlines","v":"headlines"},{"t":"t","v":" screamed. SHIPS HEADED FOR EARTH. THREE HUNDRED YEARS TO PREPARE."}],[{"t":"t","v":"At first, the world believed her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"For two days."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then a different face showed up on the news. A man with silver hair and round glasses and a quiet, serious voice. His name was Dr. Marcus Webb, and he was one of the most famous astronomers in the world. He had written three books. He had won big prizes. He had been on television hundreds of times."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And he did not believe Camila at all."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"This so-called "},{"t":"g","k":"alien","v":"alien"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":",\" Dr. Webb said calmly on the evening news, \"is not a "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":". It is a "},{"t":"g","k":"sensor","v":"sensor"},{"t":"t","v":" glitch. The Hubble "},{"t":"g","k":"telescope","v":"Telescope"},{"t":"t","v":" has had problems like this before. A young scientist saw a pattern that wasn't there, and the whole world jumped on it. I have looked at the same "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":". I see nothing.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila watched the interview from her couch at midnight. Her hands were shaking."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Her phone rang. It was Zoe."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"He's wrong,\" Zoe said. No hello. \"Cam, he is flat-out wrong.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Then why do you sound like that?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Because he's Dr. Marcus Webb. And I'm nobody.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Worst Week"}],[{"t":"t","v":"For a whole week, the world changed its mind."}],[{"t":"t","v":"News shows that had called Camila a hero now called her careless. Scientists she had admired for years said she should have checked her work better. Reporters waited outside her apartment with cameras. One of them shouted, \"Are you just making this up for attention?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"That one almost broke her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She went to the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" and sat in the dark. She pulled up the original Hubble "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":" again. She stared at the ships. They were right there. They were there. She was not making them up. She was not crazy."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But a small, ugly voice inside her head whispered, What if Webb is right, and you just can't see the mistake?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"She thought about deleting the file. She really did. If she erased the "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":", the fight would go away. She could go back to being a regular "},{"t":"g","k":"astronomer","v":"astronomer"},{"t":"t","v":". No cameras. No shouting. No silver-haired man on television saying her name like it was a joke."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Her finger hovered over the delete key for a long time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then the door opened. Kennedy walked in, carrying her tablet and two cups of coffee. She set one down next to Camila without saying a word."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy sat. She opened her tablet. She began to type."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What are you doing?\" Camila finally asked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Checking your numbers,\" Kennedy said. \"Third time.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You already checked twice.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I'm checking a third time. Because when I tell Dr. Marcus Webb he's wrong, I want to be able to look him in the eye.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila almost laughed. Almost cried. \"And if I'm wrong?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy looked up from the screen. Her face was calm, as always. \"Then we find the mistake. Together. And we fix it. Together. And the world keeps spinning. Cam, you are allowed to be wrong. You are not allowed to quit because somebody famous is mean to you on TV.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila let out a long breath she did not know she had been holding."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy went back to her screen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Numbers Do Not Lie"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy worked through the night. So did Zoe. Ava brought sandwiches. Patriya brought more coffee. Annabelle brought a stack of printed papers and a red pen and said, \"If Webb wants a fight, let's give him a fight he cannot win.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"By morning, they had a report. Forty-two pages. Every number checked. Every image verified. Every possible "},{"t":"g","k":"sensor","v":"sensor"},{"t":"t","v":" glitch ruled out."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The ships were real. The Fortitude were real."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's team published the report online for the whole world to read."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The tide turned. Slowly at first. Another scientist agreed with Camila. Then five more. Then fifty. Then the European Space Agency. Then NASA. Within two weeks, every major space agency on Earth had confirmed her work."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Dr. Marcus Webb did not say he was sorry. He did not change his mind on TV. He just went quiet for a while."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But Camila knew he had not really gone away."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Lesson"}],[{"t":"t","v":"That night, Camila walked home through the city. For the first time in weeks, no reporters followed her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava was waiting on her front steps."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You look awful,\" Ava said gently."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Thanks.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I mean it in a kind way.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila sat down next to her. For a long time, neither of them spoke."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Can I tell you something my grandmother used to say?\" Ava asked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Please.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She said: when the world tells you that you are wrong, the question is not whether you are strong enough to argue back. The question is whether you still trust what you saw with your own eyes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila nodded slowly. The city lights blinked above them. Somewhere, twenty light-years away, a "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" of ships was still coming."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I saw them, Ava. I really saw them.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"And I almost deleted the "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava put an arm around her shoulder. \"But you didn't.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Above them, the stars looked down, cold and quiet. Camila stared back at them. She thought about the three hundred years ahead."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A lot of people were going to tell her she was wrong, she realized. Maybe most of them."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She was going to have to get used to it."}]]},{"num":3,"title":"The Fortitude's Message","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" was silent except for the hum of the computer as Camila and her team waited. They had sent their message through the "},{"t":"g","k":"tiny wormhole","v":"tiny wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":" — a shortcut through space that let only signals pass through, not objects. It had taken scientists years to build, and it was still new."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The waiting felt endless. Hours turned into days. Days turned into weeks. Scientists around the world watched and listened. Then, in the middle of the night, a reply came."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A robotic, crackling voice filled the speakers."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We are the Fortitude. Our home star is dying. We need a new home. We will arrive in three hundred years.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then it stopped."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's breath caught in her throat. The Fortitude weren't explorers. They weren't curious travelers. They were desperate."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The team "},{"t":"g","k":"exchanged nervous glances","v":"exchanged nervous glances"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe was the first to speak. \"They didn't ask us for help. They didn't introduce themselves. They just told us they were coming.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy rubbed her temples. \"And that means we don't know if they plan to share Earth… or take it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The news spread fast. The world was in shock. Some saw the Fortitude as a threat. Others saw them as future "},{"t":"g","k":"allies","v":"allies"},{"t":"t","v":". "},{"t":"g","k":"governments","v":"Governments"},{"t":"t","v":" held "},{"t":"g","k":"emergency","v":"emergency"},{"t":"t","v":" meetings. Scientists "},{"t":"g","k":"debated","v":"debated"},{"t":"t","v":" how best to prepare. Some welcomed the challenge of meeting an "},{"t":"g","k":"advanced","v":"advanced"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"alien","v":"alien"},{"t":"t","v":" race. Others feared the end of human "},{"t":"g","k":"civilization","v":"civilization"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"g","k":"protests","v":"Protests"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"erupted","v":"erupted"},{"t":"t","v":" in cities around the world. Some people wanted to send "},{"t":"g","k":"weapons","v":"weapons"},{"t":"t","v":" into space. Others wanted to send "},{"t":"g","k":"peace offerings","v":"peace offerings"},{"t":"t","v":". The question on everyone's mind was the same: what would happen in three hundred years?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"In the days that followed, Camila and her team worked around the clock, analyzing the short message. Ava leaned over the console, pointing at the wave "},{"t":"g","k":"patterns","v":"patterns"},{"t":"t","v":". \"They didn't use a human language. Their message was "},{"t":"g","k":"digital","v":"digital"},{"t":"t","v":". "},{"t":"g","k":"mathematical","v":"Mathematical"},{"t":"t","v":". They understand "},{"t":"g","k":"universal patterns","v":"universal patterns"},{"t":"t","v":" — numbers, math, logic.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle frowned. \"It also means they didn't try to speak our language. That's a choice. To them, we are beneath them.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya chewed her lip. \"What if they're so intelligent they don't even see us as smart? What if, to them, we're just animals?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"That thought sent a "},{"t":"g","k":"shiver","v":"shiver"},{"t":"t","v":" down Camila's spine. The team knew they had to act fast. They had to send another message. This time, they had to make Earth's position clear."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Over the next few months, they crafted a reply. Using "},{"t":"g","k":"complex mathematical sequences","v":"complex mathematical sequences"},{"t":"t","v":", they showed Earth's technological progress, its history, and a clear statement: We are intelligent. We wish to communicate."}],[{"t":"t","v":"They hit send. And waited."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A month passed. Then, another reply arrived. This time, the voice was slower, more "},{"t":"g","k":"deliberate","v":"deliberate"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We acknowledge your intelligence. We will arrive in three "},{"t":"g","k":"centuries","v":"centuries"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The team stared at each other. No threats. No promises. Just a statement of fact."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Dr. Marcus Webb appeared on television the next morning, saying the replies could easily be faked by a computer and that the whole world was being fooled. Most people ignored him now. But Camila noticed. She always noticed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The world reacted again. People demanded answers. Was it good news? Did it mean the Fortitude saw humans as equals? Or were they still just planning to take Earth as their own?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"One thing was certain. Humanity had three "},{"t":"g","k":"centuries","v":"centuries"},{"t":"t","v":" to prepare for the most important meeting in its history."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And the clock had already started."}]]},{"num":4,"title":"The First Failure","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" was the size of a small car, and it sat in the middle of the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" like a sleeping animal."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It had taken Zoe and Kennedy eight months to build. Eight months of designs, redesigns, late nights, arguments, and coffee. Their goal was simple on paper and impossible in practice: to recreate "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion energy","v":"fusion energy"},{"t":"t","v":", the same reaction that powers the sun. If they could hold the reaction for even one minute, it would change everything."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Last check,\" Kennedy said, walking around the "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" with a tablet. \"All systems green. Containment field stable. Hydrogen feed ready.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe stood at the control panel, eyes bright. \"I've been dreaming about this for a year.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila stood behind both of them. Her stomach was tight."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Zoe,\" she said, \"if anything feels wrong — anything — we shut it down.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We will.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I mean it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know you mean it, Cam.\" Zoe grinned over her shoulder. \"Come on. Trust me.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila did trust her. That was the problem."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The decision was hers to make. The plan said they needed a full green light from the project lead before switching on. She was the project lead. She could have waited another week for the new magnetic coils Kennedy had ordered. Those new coils would have made the reaction easier to hold. But the new coils were expensive, and the project was already behind schedule, and Dr. Webb had written another "},{"t":"g","k":"editorial","v":"editorial"},{"t":"t","v":" that morning calling the whole "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" program \"a waste of public money.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila wanted a win. She wanted it badly."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Green light,\" she said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ten Seconds"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe turned the key."}],[{"t":"t","v":"At first, everything was beautiful."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A tiny star appeared inside the "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" — a bright, spinning ball of "},{"t":"g","k":"plasma","v":"plasma"},{"t":"t","v":", hotter than the surface of the sun. The "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":"'s screens lit up with green readings. Zoe let out a yell of pure joy. Kennedy smiled — her rare, small smile — and leaned closer to the observation window."}],[{"t":"t","v":"For ten seconds, the "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" ran."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then, on the second screen, one reading flickered from green to yellow."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Pressure rising on the west coil,\" Kennedy said quickly. \"It's fine. Still in range.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Yellow to orange."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Kennedy, step back from the window,\" Camila said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I'm watching the —\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Step back.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy turned to say something. And then the "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" screamed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Blast"}],[{"t":"t","v":"It wasn't a big explosion. In a movie it would have blown the roof off the building. Real "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" accidents are smaller, faster, stranger. There was a sharp crack, like a tree snapping in a storm. A flash of blue-white light. A wave of heat."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The observation window held. "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" had not been discovered yet, so the window was just thick glass and steel — but it held."}],[{"t":"t","v":"What didn't hold was a small "},{"t":"g","k":"coolant","v":"coolant"},{"t":"t","v":" pipe running above Kennedy's head. It burst. Hot steam blew down in a sudden, angry cloud."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy was closest. She threw her arm up to shield her face."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila grabbed her and pulled her back. Zoe slammed the "},{"t":"g","k":"emergency","v":"emergency"},{"t":"t","v":" shutdown. The "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" hissed and went dark. Every alarm in the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" went off at once."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Kennedy!\" Camila's voice came out shaking."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy looked down at her right arm and shoulder. The sleeve of her shirt was gone. The skin underneath was bright red, already blistering."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's not bad,\" she said, teeth clenched. \"I'm fine.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You are not fine,\" Zoe said. \"Cam, call for help. Now.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Hospital"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy spent a week in the hospital."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The burn covered most of her right shoulder and part of her upper arm. The doctors said she would heal. They also said she would carry scars for the rest of her life."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila sat by her bed on the third day. Kennedy was asleep. Her arm was wrapped in thick white bandages. A machine next to her beeped softly."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The door opened. Ava came in quietly and sat down on the other side of the bed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You can't sit out here forever, Cam,\" Ava said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Watch me.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She is going to be okay. The doctors said —\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She has scars, Ava. She will have those scars her whole life. Because of me.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava did not argue. She did not say it wasn't your fault. Ava was too honest for that. Instead she said, quietly, \"What would have happened if you had said wait another week for the new coils?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila swallowed. \"Kennedy would not be hurt.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What would Zoe have said?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She would have been annoyed. But she would have waited.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"And Dr. Webb's "},{"t":"g","k":"editorial","v":"editorial"},{"t":"t","v":"?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila was silent for a long time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"He would have written another one next month,\" she whispered. \"And another one after that.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes.\" Ava reached across the bed and took her hand. \"Cam, listen to me carefully. You made a bad call. You did. But you made it for a reason — a reason that felt real — and next time, you will weigh that reason differently. That is what a bad day is for. It teaches you something you did not know before.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It taught Kennedy something too,\" Camila said bitterly."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes. It did. And do you know what Kennedy will say when she wakes up?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She will say, let's fix it and try again. Because that is who she is. And you don't get to make her into something else just because you feel guilty.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"editorial","v":"Editorial"}],[{"t":"t","v":"The next morning, Dr. Marcus Webb's "},{"t":"g","k":"editorial","v":"editorial"},{"t":"t","v":" was on every front page."}],[{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"FUSION"},{"t":"t","v":" DISASTER: \"I TOLD YOU SO,\" SAYS WEBB."}],[{"t":"t","v":"He wrote that the project was reckless. He wrote that Camila was too young, too proud, and too eager. He wrote that Earth could not afford to put its future in the hands of a scientist who could not even protect her own team."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila read the whole thing standing in the hospital hallway."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then she read it a second time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then she folded the newspaper very carefully and put it in the trash."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy woke up an hour later."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Hey,\" Kennedy whispered."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Hey.\" Camila sat down. \"How do you feel?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Like I got hit by the sun.\" Kennedy looked at the bandages on her arm, then back up at Camila. Her eyes were tired but sharp. \"Did we get any good "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":"?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"From the "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":". Before it blew. Did we get good "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":"?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila stared at her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Cam. Did we get good "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":"?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"…Yes. A lot of it, actually. Zoe's been going through it for three days.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Good.\" Kennedy closed her eyes again. \"Then we didn't waste the burn.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila started to laugh. She did not know why. It was a strange, shaky laugh, and tears came with it. Kennedy opened one eye."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Are you crying?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"No.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You are.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I'm not.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Cam. We're going to try again. With the new coils. Right?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes. With the new coils.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Good.\" Kennedy closed her eye again. \"Tell Zoe to save all the "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":". I'm going back to sleep.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila sat there in the quiet hospital room for a long time, listening to her friend breathe."}],[{"t":"t","v":"If you stop failing, Ava had said once, you stop learning."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila had not understood the line before."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She understood it now."}]]},{"num":5,"title":"Racing Against Time","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"Camila sat in the dimly lit "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":", staring at a countdown on her screen. The number was huge — "},{"t":"g","k":"9,460,800,000 seconds","v":"9,460,800,000 seconds"},{"t":"t","v":". Three hundred years. It sounded like forever. It wasn't."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Three hundred years feels long,\" she said to her team, \"until you try to leap a thousand years of science in that time.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy nodded. She was back at work three weeks after the hospital, her arm still wrapped in a light medical sleeve under her shirt. She had not mentioned the accident once. She had not needed to. Camila saw the sleeve every day, and that was enough."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy pulled up a list of every major invention from the last three "},{"t":"g","k":"centuries","v":"centuries"},{"t":"t","v":". Steam engines. Electricity. Airplanes. Computers. Space rockets. \"All of that,\" she said, tapping the list, \"in three hundred years. We need the next three hundred to be even faster. The Fortitude may be ahead of us in almost everything. But we have one thing they might not.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Teamwork,\" Camila said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Exactly.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava leaned in. Her voice was softer than the others, but people always listened when she spoke. \"And we need to understand them. What do they need to survive? What do they care about? If we can find "},{"t":"g","k":"common ground","v":"common ground"},{"t":"t","v":", we may not need to fight at all.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe stood up and started pacing, the way she always did when her brain caught fire. \"We need power. Real power. Our best bet is still "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion energy","v":"fusion energy"},{"t":"t","v":". If we can crack it, we can run defenses, ships, even whole cities on almost nothing.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy did not flinch at the word. \"We can. With better materials.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya crossed her arms. \"Then we need stronger materials. Steel and titanium won't be enough. We need something new.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That's the problem,\" Annabelle said dryly, leaning back in her chair. \"You can't invent a material just because you need one.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Maybe we don't have to invent it,\" Patriya replied. \"Maybe it's already here. We just haven't found it yet.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"A Strange Reading from the Deep"}],[{"t":"t","v":"That was when a message blinked on Patriya's tablet. It was from a deep-sea mining ship that had been scanning the "},{"t":"g","k":"Mariana Trench","v":"Mariana Trench"},{"t":"t","v":" — the deepest place on Earth, almost seven miles down. Most of it had never been mapped."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya read the message twice. Her eyes went wide."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You're going to want to see this,\" she said quietly."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The team crowded around. The mining ship had picked up a "},{"t":"g","k":"density reading","v":"density reading"},{"t":"t","v":" from deep beneath the ocean floor. Every metal on Earth had a known density — a weight for its size. This one didn't match any of them."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's too heavy to be iron,\" Ava said, reading over her shoulder. \"Too light to be lead. And the "},{"t":"g","k":"sensor","v":"sensor"},{"t":"t","v":" says it doesn't rust, doesn't bend, and doesn't break.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy's eyebrows shot up. \"That's… impossible.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Apparently not,\" Patriya said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe stopped pacing. \"If this is real, we just found the material we need.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"If it's real,\" Annabelle said. \"And if we can get to it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"How deep is it?\" Camila asked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya hesitated. \"A mile below the seafloor. Below nearly seven miles of water.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"No one spoke for a moment."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Crushing pressure. Total darkness. Freezing cold. And a "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":" that had to reach a mile of solid rock. No "},{"t":"g","k":"submarine","v":"submarine"},{"t":"t","v":" had ever gone that deep and come back."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We'd have to design something new,\" Kennedy said slowly. \"A "},{"t":"g","k":"submarine","v":"submarine"},{"t":"t","v":" strong enough to survive the descent. A "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":" long enough to reach it. Cameras, thrusters, sensors — all of it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya's eyes gleamed. She was not afraid. She was "},{"t":"g","k":"excited","v":"excited"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Then that's what we'll build,\" she said. \"And I'll lead the mission.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila almost said no. She almost said we just had one accident; we are not ready for another. But she looked at Patriya and saw the same fire she had once seen in Zoe before the "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" test — and she understood now that fire was not the problem. Carelessness was the problem. Fire was what got you there."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Start the team,\" Camila said. \"And Patriya — we will take the time we need. However long it takes. We are not rushing this one.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya smiled. \"Understood.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Naming the Impossible"}],[{"t":"t","v":"The new metal was real. Over the next few days, the mining ship pulled up a few tiny grains — just specks — and brought them to the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":". Kennedy tested them with everything she had. A hydraulic press. A blowtorch. A diamond "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Nothing left a mark."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava whispered what the whole team was thinking. \"It's unbreakable.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy smiled. \"Then let's call it what it is.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"On the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":"'s big white board, she wrote a single word in thick black marker:"}],[{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"INDESTRUCTIUM"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"If we can pull enough of this out of the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":",\" she said, \"we can build indestructible ships. Indestructible shields. Maybe even a "},{"t":"g","k":"Dyson Sphere","v":"Dyson Sphere"},{"t":"t","v":" one day — a giant ring around the sun to drink its power.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That's a hundred years of work right there,\" Zoe said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Good,\" Camila replied. \"Because we have three hundred.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She looked at each of her teammates. "},{"t":"g","k":"engineer","v":"Engineer"},{"t":"t","v":". "},{"t":"g","k":"physicist","v":"Physicist"},{"t":"t","v":". "},{"t":"g","k":"biologist","v":"Biologist"},{"t":"t","v":". Deep-sea expert. "},{"t":"g","k":"strategist","v":"Strategist"},{"t":"t","v":". And herself — an "},{"t":"g","k":"astronomer","v":"astronomer"},{"t":"t","v":" who had started all of this by looking up."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Six women. One planet. Three "},{"t":"g","k":"centuries","v":"centuries"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The clock was ticking."}]]},{"num":6,"title":"The Deep-Sea Mission","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"submarine","v":"submarine"},{"t":"t","v":" had a name now: the Abyss Explorer. It was shaped like a thick silver teardrop, covered in the first small plates of early "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":". In the center of its belly sat the longest, thinnest "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":" ever built — a "},{"t":"g","k":"one-mile-long","v":"one-mile-long"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":" bit, coiled like a spring, that could unwind as it worked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya walked around it, tapping the hull. She grinned."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She's beautiful.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She's expensive,\" Kennedy muttered from behind her tablet. \"Try not to lose her.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya laughed. \"No promises.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The plan was simple on paper and terrifying in real life. The Abyss Explorer would sink almost seven miles down to the bottom of the "},{"t":"g","k":"Mariana Trench","v":"Mariana Trench"},{"t":"t","v":". Patriya and a two-person crew would ride inside. Once on the seafloor, they would anchor, aim the "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":", and bore a mile down through solid rock to reach the "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" deposit."}],[{"t":"t","v":"If the "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":" worked, they'd pull up the first full sample in human history."}],[{"t":"t","v":"If it didn't, they'd be the deepest-buried people in human history."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Take it slow,\" Camila said over the radio from the command center. \"We can't afford mistakes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Copy that,\" Patriya answered. \"Beginning descent.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Into the Dark"}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"submarine","v":"submarine"},{"t":"t","v":"'s engines hummed as it sank. The deeper it went, the more the sunlight faded. After a few hundred feet, the water turned deep blue. After a thousand feet, dark blue. After two thousand, pitch black. The only light came from the Abyss Explorer's own spotlights, cutting through the water like two bright swords."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy watched the readings from her seat at command. \"Pressure is increasing rapidly. Structural integrity is holding.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Translate that into human,\" Patriya joked through the static."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It means the ocean is trying to crush you and failing,\" Kennedy said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Music to my ears.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Outside the viewport, strange creatures drifted past. A pale, eyeless fish with needle teeth. A jellyfish the size of a dinner plate, glowing soft purple. A squid bigger than a bus, slipping through the darkness like a ghost."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava leaned toward the main screen in the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":", her face lit up. \"Half of these species don't have names yet. We should come back just for this.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"One impossible mission at a time,\" Annabelle said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"After nearly two hours of descent, the Abyss Explorer reached the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" floor. Patriya anchored the "},{"t":"g","k":"submarine","v":"submarine"},{"t":"t","v":" and swung the "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":" into place."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Engaging "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":",\" she announced. \"We should reach the "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" deposit in about thirty minutes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":" bit into the rock. Vibrations rolled through the "},{"t":"g","k":"submarine","v":"submarine"},{"t":"t","v":". Chunks of sediment floated upward. Minutes ticked by."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then the readings spiked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Something Down There"}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Something's wrong.\" Kennedy's voice was sharp. \"I'm picking up a "},{"t":"g","k":"massive","v":"massive"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"energy source","v":"energy source"},{"t":"t","v":" below us. Not from the "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":". From deeper.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava frowned at her own screen. \"Energy? At that depth there shouldn't be a geothermal vent for a hundred miles. There's no volcano. There's no reason for it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Suddenly the "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":" hit something harder than rock, and the "},{"t":"g","k":"submarine","v":"submarine"},{"t":"t","v":" shook violently."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Shut it down!\" Camila ordered."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya cut the power. On the screen, one small, dark, glimmering piece of "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" floated up past the camera — the first sample ever retrieved from that depth."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was smooth. It was black. And under the "},{"t":"g","k":"submarine","v":"submarine"},{"t":"t","v":"'s lights, it seemed to glow faintly from inside."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We got it,\" Patriya breathed. \"We actually got it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" below them rumbled."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A cloud of black silt boiled upward from below the "},{"t":"g","k":"drill","v":"drill"},{"t":"t","v":" site. Something inside the cloud moved — something huge."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We triggered something!\" Kennedy shouted."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's voice cracked over the radio. \"Patriya, get out of there. Now.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya engaged the thrusters. The Abyss Explorer shot upward. But the silt cloud rose with them. And behind the silt, a shape — a shadow larger than any whale, larger than any animal ever recorded — drifted up through the dark, keeping pace."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's not just a "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":",\" Ava whispered, staring at the command-center screen. \"There's something living down there.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"submarine","v":"submarine"},{"t":"t","v":" climbed. One mile. Two miles. Three. The shadow kept following — then, suddenly, stopped. As if it had hit an invisible boundary it would not cross."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya's sub shot through layer after layer of dark water until, at last, it burst through the surface in a white spray of foam."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We made it,\" she gasped. Her hands were shaking. \"We made it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"What They Brought Back"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Back at the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":", Kennedy handled the "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" sample with thick gloves. It was heavier than lead, smooth as glass. She ran every test she had on it — heat, pressure, radiation, acid. Nothing left a scratch."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's perfect,\" she said. \"If we can mine more of this, we can build ships the Fortitude can't punch through.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"But Patriya was quiet. She stood with Ava at the second screen, looking at the final scans the Abyss Explorer had sent up before escaping."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"sonar","v":"sonar"},{"t":"t","v":" images showed the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" wall. And there, carved into the rock, were long, straight lines. Too straight to be natural. Shapes that looked almost like — doors."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava's face was pale. \"Patriya… those walls. They look carved.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya nodded slowly."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila joined them. She stared at the images for a long time before speaking."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We have "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":",\" she said quietly. \"But I think we may have woken something else. And whatever it is… it's been down there a very long time.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Outside, the ocean lay calm and dark, hiding every secret it had ever kept."}]]},{"num":7,"title":"The Long Sleep","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The problem with three hundred years, Camila realized one night, was that she did not have three hundred years."}],[{"t":"t","v":"None of them did."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Even the oldest people in human history had barely lived to one hundred and twenty. The Fortitude would not arrive for three hundred. By the time the "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" entered Earth's "},{"t":"g","k":"orbit","v":"orbit"},{"t":"t","v":", Camila and her team would all be long gone — unless something changed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"That something had a name."}],[{"t":"g","k":"cryosleep","v":"Cryosleep"}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's called "},{"t":"g","k":"cryosleep","v":"cryosleep"},{"t":"t","v":",\" Dr. Harper said, her voice calm and steady as she stood in the front of the room. She was a cryobiologist — a scientist who studied how living things could survive being frozen. She had spent her entire career on this one idea. \"We put your body into a deep, cold sleep. We slow your heart down to almost nothing. We lower your body temperature to just above freezing. And we wait.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" had been turned into a briefing room for the day. The six teammates sat in folding chairs. Dr. Harper stood in front of a screen showing the inside of a "},{"t":"g","k":"cryopod","v":"cryopod"},{"t":"t","v":" — a long silver tube with a soft blue light inside."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"How long can someone stay under?\" Kennedy asked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We have safely brought people back after forty years of sleep,\" Dr. Harper said. \"Our animal tests suggest we can go much longer. Maybe sixty years. Maybe more.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila frowned. \"What's the risk?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Dr. Harper did not pretend. Camila appreciated that."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"The pods are not perfect,\" she said. \"About one pod in a hundred has a "},{"t":"g","k":"malfunction","v":"malfunction"},{"t":"t","v":" — a small error somewhere in the freezing or the waking. Most of those are minor. A few have been serious. We are getting better every year. But I will not lie to you. Going into a "},{"t":"g","k":"cryopod","v":"cryopod"},{"t":"t","v":" is not the same as going to sleep at night. Things can go wrong.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya was the first to speak. \"And if we don't do it?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Dr. Harper's face grew kinder. \"Then you will live your lives. You will do wonderful work. And the Fortitude will arrive a hundred and fifty years after you die. Your team will hand the mission to someone else. Someone who was not there at the beginning.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The room was quiet."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Decision"}],[{"t":"t","v":"That night, the six of them sat in their old "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":", the one with the scuffed floor and the whiteboard that still had "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"INDESTRUCTIUM"},{"t":"t","v":" written in the corner in Kennedy's handwriting."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Nobody wanted to speak first."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Finally, Zoe said, \"I hate this.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Which part?\" Ava asked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"All of it. The pods. The risk. The idea that I am going to close my eyes and when I open them, everyone I know outside this room is old or gone. My parents. My sister. My nieces.\" Zoe's voice cracked on the last word. \"My niece is four, guys. I am supposed to watch her grow up.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You can still watch her grow up,\" Annabelle said quietly. \"Just differently. She will be older than you one day. You will be aunts in reverse.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That is not comforting.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I wasn't trying to comfort you. I was trying to be accurate.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava let out a small laugh."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila rubbed her eyes. \"I think we have to do it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"They all looked at her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"If we do not,\" she said slowly, \"we spend the next forty years working our hardest — and then we pass the work to strangers. Good strangers, probably. Smart strangers. But strangers. Who will not remember why we started. Who will not remember Kennedy's arm, or Patriya's shadow in the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":", or the first night we heard the Fortitude's voice.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Our kids could remember,\" Patriya said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"If we have kids. And if they choose to take up the mission. Patriya, my mother was a doctor. I became an "},{"t":"g","k":"astronomer","v":"astronomer"},{"t":"t","v":". My kids would become whatever they wanted. I would want them to.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"So we sleep,\" Kennedy said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We sleep in pieces,\" Camila said. \"Not three hundred years at once. That is too long and too risky. We wake up every thirty or forty years. When the world needs us. When a decision is big enough that the six of us should be in the room. And in between, we sleep.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She looked around at her team. \"I am not going to tell any of you what to do. This has to be your choice. Your own. I will understand completely if any of you say no.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"For a long minute, no one spoke."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then Ava said, \"I'm in.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"In,\" Kennedy said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"In,\" Zoe whispered, wiping her face."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"In,\" Patriya said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Obviously in,\" Annabelle said. \"Someone has to keep the rest of you out of trouble across the "},{"t":"g","k":"centuries","v":"centuries"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila let out a breath she had not known she was holding."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Then we sleep.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Goodbyes"}],[{"t":"t","v":"The weeks before the first "},{"t":"g","k":"cryosleep","v":"cryosleep"},{"t":"t","v":" were the strangest of Camila's life."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She visited her mother. They baked cookies together, the way they had when Camila was a girl. Her mother was brave about it. She kept saying, \"I am proud of you, mija. I am so proud.\" Neither of them cried until Camila was in the car driving away."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She wrote letters. Dozens of letters. To her brother. To her childhood best friend. To a teacher who had told her, long ago, that she should study the stars. She told each of them that when they read the letters, she would already be asleep. She told them not to be sad. She told them to live good lives. She told them she would think of them, someday, when she woke up."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe spent two weeks with her niece. She took her to the zoo. She took her for ice cream. She told her about the stars. The little girl did not fully understand what was happening. Zoe said that was fine. She kissed the top of her head and told her she would always be her auntie, no matter what."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy visited her parents' graves. They had both passed away years before. She sat on the grass for a long time and said nothing at all."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Pod"}],[{"t":"t","v":"On the morning of the first sleep, the six of them walked together into a large, cold room lined with six silver pods."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Dr. Harper and a small team were waiting. There were checks to run, papers to sign, sensors to attach. It took hours. No one rushed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"At last, Camila stood beside her pod. She was wearing a plain gray jumpsuit. Her hair was tied back. Her hands were shaking a little."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Forty years,\" Dr. Harper said gently. \"We will wake you when the world needs you. Or sooner, if anything goes wrong.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila nodded."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She looked down the row. Zoe was already lying in her pod, eyes closed, mouth pressed tight. Kennedy was sitting on the edge of hers, rubbing her scarred arm through her sleeve — the habit she had when she was nervous. Ava was smiling, calm as ever. Patriya gave Camila a thumbs up. Annabelle winked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila climbed in."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The pod was softer than it looked. Cool, not cold. Lights dimmed. A hiss of gas filled the chamber. Camila's eyelids grew heavy."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Her last thought before sleep was of her mother's kitchen. Warm. Full of the smell of cookies. Her mother laughing at something Camila had said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then everything went quiet."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Waking Up"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Waking up was nothing like sleep."}],[{"t":"t","v":"There was no slow drift, no gentle morning. One moment Camila was nowhere at all. The next, she was gasping. Light. Noise. A voice saying her name."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Camila. Camila. Come on back. You're okay. You're okay.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She opened her eyes."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Dr. Harper's face was above hers. But it was not Dr. Harper. This woman was older. Much older. Gray-haired. Kind eyes. She looked a little bit like Dr. Harper, but she was not."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I'm Dr. Harper,\" the woman said softly. \"My name is Lila Harper. My grandmother was the one who put you under.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila stared at her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"How long?\" she whispered."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Forty-one years,\" the younger Dr. Harper said. \"Welcome back, Dr. Reyes. The world has changed a lot.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila turned her head. The other pods were opening one by one. Zoe. Kennedy. Ava. Patriya. Annabelle. All of them. All six. All okay."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She closed her eyes for a moment. All six. Thank you. Thank you. Thank you."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A new assistant stepped forward with a tablet. \"Dr. Reyes, there are some things you should know. The "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" program has made huge progress — Dr. Zoe's notes were copied and studied for decades. "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" mining has expanded. "},{"t":"g","k":"the Fortitude Accord","v":"The Fortitude Accord"},{"t":"t","v":" is…\" The assistant paused. \"Complicated. We'll go through it slowly.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila cleared her throat. Her voice was rough from forty years of not being used. \"And Dr. Marcus Webb?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The assistant blinked. \"Sir, Dr. Webb is — I mean, ma'am, sorry — Dr. Webb is still alive. He is ninety-four years old. He retired long ago. But he is still writing articles about the Fortitude program. He has written about a thousand of them over the years. He is very consistent.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila closed her eyes again. A tiny, tired smile pulled at the corner of her mouth."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Some things, she thought, do not change."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Outside the "},{"t":"g","k":"cryopod","v":"cryopod"},{"t":"t","v":" room, the world that had slept without her for forty-one years was waiting."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was time to get back to work."}]]},{"num":8,"title":"Secrets of the Stars","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"For months after the first wake-up, the team ran two projects side by side. Upstairs, Zoe and Kennedy worked on "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion power","v":"fusion power"},{"t":"t","v":". Downstairs, Ava and her new team of linguists tried to "},{"t":"g","k":"decode","v":"decode"},{"t":"t","v":" the Fortitude's language. And somewhere on a screen in the back of the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":", a blinking dot marked the deep-sea "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" sensors — still pulsing, still alive."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila moved between all three. She barely slept."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Which, her team liked to remind her, was funny, considering she had just slept for forty years."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"Fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" Problem"}],[{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"Fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" was the same reaction that made stars shine. Squeeze two hydrogen atoms together hard enough, and they fuse into helium, releasing a huge burst of energy. A cup of seawater could, in theory, power a city for a year."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The trouble was still holding the reaction. Forty years of other scientists had not solved it."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's like juggling the sun,\" Zoe said one morning, staring at a holographic model of a "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":". The glowing "},{"t":"g","k":"plasma","v":"plasma"},{"t":"t","v":" inside spun faster and faster, then collapsed. \"Every time we get it going, the containment fails. The "},{"t":"g","k":"plasma","v":"plasma"},{"t":"t","v":" eats through the walls.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Any material we build with melts,\" Kennedy agreed. \"Steel melts. Tungsten melts. Even our best ceramics melt.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe stopped pacing. Her eyes lit up."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What doesn't melt?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy stared at her. Then she said the word they were both thinking."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\""},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"They spent three weeks building a new "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" core. A thin shell of "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":", grown molecule by molecule, wrapped around a chamber the size of a basketball. Kennedy ran every safety check twice — and then three times. She would not be rushed. Camila, watching her, did not say a word. She just nodded every time Kennedy asked for another day."}],[{"t":"t","v":"When they finally turned it on, the "},{"t":"g","k":"plasma","v":"plasma"},{"t":"t","v":" inside spun like a tiny, furious star."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And it held."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It held for one second. Then ten. Then a minute. Then an hour."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" didn't just work. It produced ten times the energy any previous "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" had managed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy watched the readings and slowly sat down. \"This changes everything.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It changes everything,\" Zoe agreed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila let herself smile. And for the first time in a long time, when she thought of Kennedy's scars, she did not feel guilty. She felt proud."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Learning to Listen"}],[{"t":"t","v":"While Zoe and Kennedy celebrated, Ava was hunched in a separate room, surrounded by screens full of scrolling "},{"t":"g","k":"alien","v":"alien"},{"t":"t","v":" symbols. Her team had recorded every signal the Fortitude had sent — and every signal the Fortitude had sent to each other as the "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" moved closer."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Fortitude did not speak in words. They spoke in "},{"t":"g","k":"patterns","v":"patterns"},{"t":"t","v":" — short bursts of numbers that formed images, diagrams, and commands."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's like a puzzle,\" Ava explained to Camila one evening. \"Each burst is a picture. Each picture is a word. But the rules of how the pictures fit together are different from any language on Earth.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Why?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava hesitated. \"Because they don't ask questions. Their language has no word for maybe. No word for please. Every sentence is a command, or a fact, or a coordinate.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila frowned. \"A whole "},{"t":"g","k":"civilization","v":"civilization"},{"t":"t","v":" without maybe?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That's what the "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":" says.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle, listening from the doorway, smirked. \"A "},{"t":"g","k":"civilization","v":"civilization"},{"t":"t","v":" that can't say 'maybe' is going to be really bad at surprises.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila made a note of that. It felt important."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Pulse Beneath the Sea"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya came in near midnight. She wasn't grinning anymore."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You all need to come see the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"They followed her down to the ocean research "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":". A big dark screen showed a long, quiet line of white noise — the sound of the deep ocean turned into light. Every few seconds, a small spike appeared."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then another."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then another."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"At first I thought it was just "},{"t":"g","k":"sonar","v":"sonar"},{"t":"t","v":" echoes,\" Patriya said. \"But look.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She zoomed in. The spikes were not random. They came in groups of three. Then groups of five. Then groups of three again. Over and over."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava stared. \"That's a pattern.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\""},{"t":"g","k":"patterns","v":"Patterns"},{"t":"t","v":" don't make themselves,\" Patriya said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy tapped the screen. \"Could it be a whale? Whales make "},{"t":"g","k":"patterns","v":"patterns"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Not at this frequency. Not at this depth. And not in the same pattern every time.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe leaned in. \"So something down there is sending a signal. On purpose.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila felt the same chill she had felt when the Fortitude message first reached Earth. \"Is it aimed at the Fortitude?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I can't tell,\" Patriya admitted. \"The signal isn't going up. It's just… pulsing. Like a heartbeat.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle folded her arms. \"Or like someone tapping on a wall, waiting to see if anyone taps back.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"No one laughed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila stared at the screen for a long moment. \"We have two mysteries now. The ones coming from the stars — and the ones that might already be here.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She looked at her team."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We do not tell anyone about this second one. Not yet. Not until we know what we're dealing with.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Everyone nodded."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Above them, a "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" was racing through space."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Below them, something was tapping on a wall."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And between them, six women were trying to figure out which one was more dangerous."}]]},{"num":9,"title":"A Voice in the Dark","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"Ava quit on a Tuesday."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She did not send an angry message. She did not write a long explanation. She walked into Camila's office, set down her badge, and said, \"I cannot do this anymore. I'm sorry.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then she left."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila did not try to stop her. She watched her friend walk out the door, and then she sat very still for a long time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Why She Quit"}],[{"t":"t","v":"For two years, Ava had been trying to crack the deepest layer of the Fortitude language — the one that held real names, real places, real feelings. Words, not just numbers. Her team had decoded hundreds of commands and coordinates. But whenever they tried to pull a name out of the "},{"t":"g","k":"alien","v":"alien"},{"t":"t","v":" code, the pattern shattered. Nothing fit."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Two years of sixteen-hour days. Two years of sleeping in the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":". Two years of being almost there."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And nothing to show for it."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava had been the steady one. Ava was the person who told other people, failure is how we learn. Ava was the one who had held Camila's hand in the hospital. Seeing her walk out was like watching a wall you thought was concrete turn out to be paper."}],[{"t":"t","v":"That night, Camila drove to Ava's house."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Kitchen Table"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava opened the door before Camila could knock."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I figured you'd show up,\" Ava said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Of course I showed up.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Don't try to talk me out of it, Cam.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I'm not going to.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava paused. That had not been the answer she expected. She stepped back from the door. \"Come in, then.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"They sat at Ava's kitchen table. Ava's house was small and quiet, full of plants and books. A teakettle whistled on the stove. Ava poured two cups. Neither of them spoke for a long time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Finally, Camila said, \"Tell me what's actually wrong.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava stared at her tea."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I am tired, Cam.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"No. I mean I am tired. Deep in my bones tired. I have not laughed in six months. I do not remember the last time I read a book for fun. I talk to "},{"t":"g","k":"alien","v":"alien"},{"t":"t","v":" code in my sleep. And every morning I get up and I go do it again because I am afraid that if I take one single day off, the Fortitude will arrive and it will be my fault that we do not understand what they are saying.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That is a lot to carry.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It is too much to carry.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila nodded. She did not say you're being too hard on yourself. She had been told that a hundred times by well-meaning people after Kennedy's accident, and it had never once helped."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Instead she said, \"What would make it bearable?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava looked up. \"What?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"If you came back. What would make it bearable? Not what would make it perfect. Not what would fix it. What would make it bearable.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava thought for a long time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I would need help,\" she said slowly. \"I would need someone else to be the face of the project. Someone else who answers to the "},{"t":"g","k":"governments","v":"governments"},{"t":"t","v":". Someone else who takes the calls at two in the morning. I cannot do that part anymore. I can still do the work. But I cannot be in charge of it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Then I will do that part.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Cam, you already have five other jobs.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I will do that part. I will find someone full-time, and I will be the bridge until we do. Deal?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava smiled — really smiled — for the first time in a year. \"Deal.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"And one more thing,\" Camila said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You are taking two weeks off. Right now. Starting tomorrow. Go somewhere with no screens.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Cam, I can't —\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You can. You will. That is an order from your friend.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava laughed. It was a small laugh, but it was real."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Breakthrough"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Three weeks later, Ava came back."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She looked different. Her hair was shorter. Her eyes were brighter. She walked into the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" carrying a cup of coffee and a notebook full of handwritten notes."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I saw something,\" she said. \"On vacation. I was watching the ocean, and I saw something.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"The waves come in groups. Not random. Sets of three small, then two big. Sets of five, then one. Human ears stop hearing it after a while because we are used to it. But if you count, the pattern is there. The ocean has its own math.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Ava, what does that have to do with —\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"The Fortitude language has background waves, Cam. All this time I have been trying to "},{"t":"g","k":"decode","v":"decode"},{"t":"t","v":" the loud bursts. The shouts. But there are tiny, quiet signals between the bursts. I ignored them. My whole team ignored them. We thought they were noise. They are not noise. They are the soft parts. They are where the names live.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava opened her notebook. She showed Camila a long list of freshly decoded symbols."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Half of them were words Camila had never seen before."}],[{"t":"t","v":"One of them was a name."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen"}],[{"t":"t","v":"The name was Valen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was the only name in the whole first batch. The rest were things like coordinate, "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":", engine, hull. But Valen — Valen was a person. A specific Fortitude. A "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She is the one,\" Ava said softly. \"She is the one who has been sending the replies.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila stared at the screen. \"A "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":". A Fortitude "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Which means… she has been studying us. Our language. Our signals. Probably for decades.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Which means if any single Fortitude out there knows anything about human beings…\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It is her.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila felt something shift inside her chest. For the first time, the Fortitude were not a "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":". They were not a wall of ships twenty light-years away. One of them was a person, with a name, and that person had been reading Earth's mail."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Ava,\" Camila said, \"can we send her a message? Just to her?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We can try.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What would we say?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava smiled. \"How about 'hello'?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Across the Void"}],[{"t":"t","v":"They sent the message that night."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was three symbols, in Ava's newly decoded script."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Hello, Valen. My name is Camila."}],[{"t":"t","v":"For a week, there was no reply."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then, late on a Thursday evening, the "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":" console chimed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A single line appeared on the screen, translated in real time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Hello, Camila. I was not sure you would ever see me."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila read the words three times. Her hands were shaking a little. Across the room, Ava was smiling, tears in her eyes."}],[{"t":"t","v":"For the first time in three hundred years of fear, a human and a Fortitude had spoken."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Not across a battlefield."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Just across a table."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Reply,\" Ava whispered."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's fingers hovered over the keyboard. Slowly, carefully, she typed:"}],[{"t":"t","v":"We see you. We have been seeing you for a long time. Would you like to talk?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"She hit send."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":" hummed. Somewhere, twenty light-years away, a Fortitude "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":" named Valen was about to answer."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The clock was still ticking."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But for the first time in a long time, it felt like it might be ticking toward something — not just away."}]]},{"num":10,"title":"The Fortitude's Weakness","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The next "},{"t":"g","k":"cryosleep","v":"cryosleep"},{"t":"t","v":" cycle had come and gone. Camila was older now — small gray streaks in her dark hair, fine lines at the corners of her eyes. She still worked fourteen-hour days. She still drank too much coffee. Some things "},{"t":"g","k":"cryosleep","v":"cryosleep"},{"t":"t","v":" did not change."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The breakthrough came from a small thing."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila was reviewing months of intercepted Fortitude messages when she noticed something strange — not about what the aliens said, but about how they said it."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Every message is a command,\" she said, tapping her screen. \"Every reply is an acknowledgment. No one ever argues. No one ever asks for help.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle, seated across from her, looked up. \"So?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"So on Earth, even the best teams argue. Scientists argue. Kids on a soccer team argue. My mom and I argue about dishes. Arguing is how humans fix ideas.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You're saying the Fortitude don't fix each other's mistakes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I'm saying they may not know how to.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle set down her coffee. Now she was interested."}],[{"t":"t","v":"They pulled the rest of the team in."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Missing Word"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava confirmed it from her own work. \"Their language doesn't have a word for help. It doesn't have a word for together. It doesn't even have a word for friend. When I mapped every word we've decoded, ninety percent of them were orders or numbers.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy's eyes narrowed. \"A military culture?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Deeper than that,\" Ava said. \"I think every Fortitude is expected to do one job, perfectly, alone. No teams. No collaboration. Just a long chain of commands.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya leaned in. \"That might explain why they survived. If their planet was harsh, only the strongest lived. Only the ones who didn't need anyone.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"But we're not harsh,\" Camila said slowly. \"We're messy. We have ten different ways to do one thing. Our teams argue, and out of that arguing, new ideas appear. They don't do that.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe caught up fast. \"So their whole way of fighting a battle assumes the plan works.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Exactly,\" Camila said. \"They've probably never had to improvise under pressure. Not really.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava hesitated. \"Except maybe Valen.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The room went quiet."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila had been writing to Valen now for almost two years — short messages, careful exchanges, slowly building up. Valen was different from the other Fortitude. She asked questions. She used soft words. She had learned what hello meant, and what friend meant, and she had started using them."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But Valen was one Fortitude. One. Out of millions."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We do not plan the defense around Valen,\" Camila said gently. \"We plan it around what the "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" as a whole is likely to do. Valen is an exception. We hope.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava nodded. \"Right. Of course.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle stood up. She was already grinning — that sharp, dangerous grin she got when she saw the answer to a problem three steps ahead of everyone else. \"Okay. So that's the weakness. Let's use it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle's Plan"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Over the next week, Annabelle sketched out what she called the "},{"t":"g","k":"Chaos Plan","v":"Chaos Plan"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It had three parts."}],[{"t":"t","v":"First, jam their messages. Kennedy's engineers were already building "},{"t":"g","k":"electromagnetic disruptors","v":"electromagnetic disruptors"},{"t":"t","v":" — devices that could fill the air with static and noise on the exact "},{"t":"g","k":"frequencies","v":"frequencies"},{"t":"t","v":" the Fortitude used to talk to each other. Without clear orders, Fortitude ships would be like soldiers in a battle wearing blindfolds."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Second, flood them with choices. Instead of fighting in one giant line, Earth would split its defense into hundreds of small, fast teams, each making its own decisions. The Fortitude would not know who to attack first. They would have to pick targets on the fly — and picking on the fly was exactly what they weren't trained to do."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Third, make them doubt each other. Ava's team would craft "},{"t":"g","k":"fake","v":"fake"},{"t":"t","v":" Fortitude messages using the language they were decoding. In the middle of a battle, Earth could send a false order — \"retreat,\" \"re-target,\" \"stand down\" — in the Fortitude's own code. Even a few seconds of confusion could turn a battle."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's asymmetric,\" Annabelle said. \"We don't need to be stronger than they are. We just need to be messier than they can handle.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy let out a low whistle. \"That's actually brilliant.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya grinned. \"That's actually sneaky.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That's actually humans,\" Ava said, smiling. \"That's exactly what we are.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Humanity, Together"}],[{"t":"t","v":"There was one more piece. The biggest one."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"The plan only works if the whole planet fights as a single team,\" Annabelle said. \"If one country sits out, the Fortitude find a hole and pour through it. We've never done that. Ever. In all of human history.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"For a long minute, no one spoke."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then Camila said, \"Then we make it the first time.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"It took two years of meetings. Two years of speeches and arguments and late-night video calls with every government on Earth. Old rivals sat at the same tables. Countries that had not spoken in decades had to agree on how to share technology, ships, and scientists."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was ugly. It was slow. It was loud."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But it almost worked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"On a rainy morning in New York, nearly every nation on Earth signed a single agreement: "},{"t":"g","k":"the Fortitude Accord","v":"the Fortitude Accord"},{"t":"t","v":". One plan. One defense. One planet."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Almost."}],[{"t":"t","v":"One country had refused to sign."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila watched the ceremony on a screen in the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":", her team beside her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You know,\" Zoe said quietly, \"maybe the Fortitude did us a favor.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy raised an eyebrow. \"How do you figure?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We've spent our whole history fighting each other. They gave us one reason to stop.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Almost,\" Camila said softly. Her eyes were on the one empty chair at the signing table — the chair for the country that had walked away. \"Almost.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Above, the stars were quiet."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Below, in the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":", the pulse was still tapping."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Three. Five. Three. Five."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Like a heartbeat."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Like someone waiting to be noticed."}]]},{"num":11,"title":"The Holdout and the Saboteur","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The country that had refused to sign the "},{"t":"g","k":"Accord","v":"Accord"},{"t":"t","v":" was called Ardana."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was not a huge country. It did not have the biggest army or the most scientists. But it had one thing every other country needed: the largest "},{"t":"g","k":"lithium","v":"lithium"},{"t":"t","v":" mines in the world. Every "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"shipyard","v":"shipyard"},{"t":"t","v":", every "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":", every "},{"t":"g","k":"disruptor","v":"disruptor"},{"t":"t","v":" tower ran on batteries that needed Ardanian "},{"t":"g","k":"lithium","v":"lithium"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"If Ardana sat out the defense, Earth's whole plan had a hole in it."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ardana's president was a woman named President Osei. She had been in power for nine years. She was popular at home. And she was famously hard to move."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Cam,\" Annabelle said one morning. \"We have to go to her.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You. In person. The video calls aren't working. She keeps saying we are treating her country like a tool, not like a partner. She's not wrong. Somebody has to sit across a table from her and listen.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I am a scientist, Annabelle. Not a "},{"t":"g","k":"diplomat","v":"diplomat"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She has met twelve diplomats already. She has not met you. You are the face of this entire mission. If you go, it means something.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila let out a long breath. \"I'm going to be terrible at this.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Probably,\" Annabelle said. \"So I'm going with you. I'll be in your earpiece the whole time. You talk. I'll help you hear what she is really saying.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Meeting"}],[{"t":"t","v":"The flight to Ardana took eleven hours. Camila did not sleep."}],[{"t":"t","v":"President Osei met her in a small room in the presidential palace. Just the two of them. No cameras. No advisors. Osei was in her sixties, with gray hair cut short and sharp brown eyes. She did not smile."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Dr. Reyes,\" she said, shaking Camila's hand. \"Welcome to Ardana. Sit.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila sat. Annabelle's voice was a soft hum in her ear."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Listen first, Cam. Don't pitch. Listen.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Madame President,\" Camila began. \"Thank you for seeing me. I'm not going to give you a speech. I would like to ask you a question instead, if that's all right.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Osei raised an eyebrow. \"Go on.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Why is your country the one saying no?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"There was a long silence."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then Osei leaned back in her chair."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Because for three hundred years,\" she said, \"every time the world has needed something from Ardana, the world has come to take it. It came for our rubber. Then our diamonds. Then our oil. Now it comes for our "},{"t":"g","k":"lithium","v":"lithium"},{"t":"t","v":". And every time, the world promises partnership. And every time, when the need is over, the world leaves. Ardana gives. The world gets richer. Ardana stays the same.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila was quiet."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"So when I hear the words Fortitude "},{"t":"g","k":"Accord","v":"Accord"},{"t":"t","v":",\" Osei continued, \"I hear another version of that story. Your ships. Our batteries. Your decisions. Our labor. And when the Fortitude are gone, you will forget us again. Tell me I am wrong, Dr. Reyes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"She isn't wrong,\" Annabelle whispered in the earpiece. \"Don't argue. Agree.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's mouth was dry. She wanted to defend the mission. She wanted to say this time is different. But Annabelle was right. If she said this time is different, she would sound like every other person who had ever come to take something from Ardana."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She chose instead to tell the truth."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Madame President, you are not wrong. You are not wrong. And I am not going to sit here and try to convince you that I am somehow better than every other person who has ever made promises to your country. I probably am not.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Osei's eyebrow went up a little further."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What I can tell you,\" Camila said, \"is that I have made a lot of mistakes. I almost quit after my first big discovery. I burned my best friend in a "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" accident because I wanted a win more than I wanted to be careful. I have been doubted by an entire planet and I have been too stubborn to listen when I should have. I am not a great leader. I am a scientist who keeps trying.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She looked Osei in the eye."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"If Ardana signs, Ardana should sign as an equal. With a seat at the table every time a decision is made. Not just when the batteries are needed. Your scientists in our labs. Your ships in our "},{"t":"g","k":"orbit","v":"orbit"},{"t":"t","v":". Your name on every ship we build with your metal. And if, when this is over, the world tries to leave you behind again — I will personally come back here and stand with you.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Osei did not answer for a long time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Those are easy words, Dr. Reyes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Words are what every other person has given me.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Osei tapped her fingers on the table. \"Why should I believe you?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You shouldn't. Not yet. You should test me. Write whatever conditions you want into the "},{"t":"g","k":"Accord","v":"Accord"},{"t":"t","v":". Any conditions. Every condition. Make them binding. Make them embarrassing if we break them. And if we refuse even one, you walk.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle's voice was crackling in Camila's ear now. \"Cam. Cam. You are going way past what any of us agreed you could offer.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila ignored her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Osei tilted her head. \"Any conditions?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Any conditions.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That,\" Osei said slowly, \"is not how diplomats talk.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I told you. I'm not a "},{"t":"g","k":"diplomat","v":"diplomat"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"For the first time, President Osei almost smiled."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Draft the conditions,\" Osei said. \"Both of us. Together. Starting tomorrow. If your team agrees to what we write, Ardana signs.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila let out a breath. \"Thank you.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Do not thank me yet, Dr. Reyes. Many of these conditions will be uncomfortable.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Good,\" Camila said. \"Discomfort is how we learn.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Sabotage"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ardana signed two months later."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The full Fortitude "},{"t":"g","k":"Accord","v":"Accord"},{"t":"t","v":" was complete. Every nation. One plan. One defense. One planet. It was the biggest agreement in human history."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It lasted six weeks."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then a "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" in the desert blew up."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Not like Camila's old one. This one was bigger — a real, city-scale "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":", powering a whole defense grid. The explosion did not kill anyone. But it destroyed eight months of work and ten years of parts."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was not an accident."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Investigators found a small device in the wreckage — a timer, carefully placed. Someone had walked in, set the timer, walked out. Someone who knew where to plant it. Someone inside the program."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila read the report in silence. Then she called Annabelle."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Annabelle. Look at the guest list from the "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":"'s last inspection. Who had access?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle's voice came back slowly. \"Cam. Dr. Marcus Webb was on that list. As a retired advisor. He walks through once a quarter.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila closed her eyes."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I want to talk to him.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Old Man"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Dr. Webb was ninety-four years old. He lived alone in a house by the sea."}],[{"t":"t","v":"He answered the door himself. He was smaller than Camila remembered. His silver hair had gone white. He walked slowly, leaning on a cane. But his eyes, behind the same round glasses, were as sharp as ever."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I thought you would come eventually,\" he said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Did you do it?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"No.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Can you prove that?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"No.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila sat down across from him in his little living room. The windows looked out over the ocean. A cup of tea steamed on the table."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Dr. Webb. A "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" was destroyed. The device was placed by someone who knew the site. You are one of a small number of people who have access.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"So you understand why I'm here.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes. I do.\" Webb looked down at his hands. \"I did not plant the device, Dr. Reyes. I swear that on my life. I have not set foot in that facility for four months. You can check every camera. You will find I am telling the truth.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Then why am I here?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Webb was quiet for a long, long time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Because,\" he said finally, \"the person who did plant it is almost certainly someone who read my work.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila did not speak."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I have been writing for sixty years,\" Webb said slowly, \"that your program is reckless. That the Fortitude may not even be real. That the money could be spent better. I have been wrong, Dr. Reyes. I have been wrong from the beginning. I know that now. But I was stubborn. And famous. And I have an audience. I have had an audience for half a "},{"t":"g","k":"century","v":"century"},{"t":"t","v":". And somewhere out there, somebody read my articles their whole life — and decided to do something about it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's throat was tight."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I did not light the match,\" Webb said. \"But I spent sixty years leaving gasoline around.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"He looked up at her. His eyes were wet."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I am not going to say I am sorry. I do not think I deserve to. But I am going to stop. Today. I will not write another word against your program. I will not say another word against you. It is too late to make up for what I have done. But I can stop making it worse.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila sat very still. She did not know what to feel. She had hated this man, quietly, for decades. She had used his name as a reason to push too hard, too fast. Kennedy's scars were, in a way, partly his."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But he was also an old man in a small house by the sea, telling her the truth."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Dr. Webb.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Thank you for telling me.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"He nodded."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"And for what it's worth,\" she said, standing up, \"I am sorry it took you sixty years. But I am glad it took only sixty.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"A small, tired smile pulled at his mouth."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You are kinder than I deserve, Dr. Reyes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I learned it from someone kind.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She walked out."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The investigators eventually caught the "},{"t":"g","k":"saboteur","v":"saboteur"},{"t":"t","v":" — a young man, angry, raised on old editorials, convinced he was saving Earth from a lie. He was arrested without anyone being hurt. The "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" was rebuilt. Life went on."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Dr. Marcus Webb died peacefully two years later, in his sleep."}],[{"t":"t","v":"He did not write a single word against Camila's program in those last two years."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Not one."}]]},{"num":12,"title":"The Battle Plan","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The years began to blur."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The first "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"shipyard","v":"shipyard"},{"t":"t","v":" opened in low "},{"t":"g","k":"orbit","v":"orbit"},{"t":"t","v":" — a giant, silvery ring that built ships without gravity to get in the way. The first full-scale "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" ship, the "},{"t":"g","k":"ISV Pioneer","v":"ISV Pioneer"},{"t":"t","v":", rolled off the line and took her first flight around the moon without a single scratch. Then came a second. Then ten. Then a hundred."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The first "},{"t":"g","k":"fusion","v":"fusion"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"reactor","v":"reactor"},{"t":"t","v":" powered the city of Tokyo."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The first Earth-wide defense grid came online, stitching together radar, lasers, and Annabelle's jamming fields into one enormous net."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The team slept again. And again. And again. Each time, they woke a little older. Each time, a few more human lifetimes had passed outside. Each time, the Fortitude "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" was closer."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And each time, Camila wrote to Valen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Room Where It Was Decided"}],[{"t":"t","v":"When the Fortitude were just a few years out, Camila called her team to the old "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" — the same room where she had first seen the ships on her screen. It felt smaller now. They were older. Their hair had more gray in it. But it was still them."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Before we do anything else,\" Camila said, \"we need to agree on one question. Do we shoot? Or do we talk?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We do both,\" Annabelle said at once."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava shook her head. \"We can do both. But we don't have to lead with war. If we point a gun at them the moment they arrive, we get a fight no matter what.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"And if we don't point a gun at all, we get one anyway,\" Annabelle answered. \"The gun has to exist. What matters is whether we pull the trigger.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe leaned forward. \"What if we show them the gun — and then show them a table?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"They all looked at her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We say: we could fight you. We would lose some, you would lose some. Or we could help you. Here is another planet. Here is the technology to make it livable. Choose.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy nodded slowly. \"That's strength and kindness at the same time.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That's the offer,\" Camila agreed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Three Scenarios"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Before sending the message, they mapped the three futures the world might face."}],[{"t":"t","v":"One: the Fortitude say yes. They accept the offer and take a new planet. Humanity helps them "},{"t":"g","k":"terraform","v":"terraform"},{"t":"t","v":" it — turn it from a dead rock into a livable world. Peace."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Two: the Fortitude say no. They come for Earth anyway. The "},{"t":"g","k":"Accord","v":"Accord"},{"t":"t","v":" activates. "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" ships meet them in "},{"t":"g","k":"orbit","v":"orbit"},{"t":"t","v":". Disruption fields scramble their orders. Humanity fights the messiest, most confusing battle any army has ever fought, and hopes its messiness is enough."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Three: the Fortitude say yes — and lie. They pretend to agree, then attack when Earth lowers its guard."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That last one is what I'd do,\" Annabelle said quietly, \"if I were them.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That's why we never lower our guard,\" Camila said. \"We help them. But we don't trust them. Not until the very last one of them is on their new world.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She paused. \"Except Valen. I trust Valen.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle looked at her carefully. \"Cam. I have to say this. You have been writing to Valen for almost a hundred years now — in bursts, on and off, between sleeps. I know you feel like you know her. But she is one Fortitude. You do not plan a planetary defense around one friend.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Do you?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes,\" Camila said. \"I do. I am not going to let Valen decide this for us. The message we send to the "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" will be firm. It will be for everyone. But if it reaches her first — and it probably will, since she is the "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":" — then maybe we get lucky. Maybe she helps the others understand us.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle studied her for a moment, then nodded. \"Okay. That I can live with.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Message"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila wrote it herself."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She wrote it in the Fortitude's own symbols, using everything Ava's team had decoded. She wrote it short, because short was how the Fortitude spoke."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It said:"}],[{"t":"t","v":"We understand. Your star is dying. You need a home."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Earth is ours."}],[{"t":"t","v":"We can defend it. We have the ships. We have the energy. We have the unity."}],[{"t":"t","v":"We offer a better path. Help us find you a new planet — and we will help you settle it. Together, we build instead of burn."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Answer."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She sent it through the "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then they waited."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Hours. A day. A second day."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" did not empty. No one wanted to miss the answer."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Late on the second night, the "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":" crackled."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A deep, metallic voice filled the room — not Valen's soft written reply, but the voice of the "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" itself."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We acknowledge your strength. We acknowledge your offer. We will discuss.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Silence."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy was the first to exhale. \"They're not saying no.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"They're not saying yes either,\" Annabelle said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava looked at Camila. \"But they're talking. A hundred years ago they wouldn't even use the word offer. Now they are. That's a change.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila nodded. Her heart was pounding. \"It's the first time in their entire history they've had to choose. Let's give them room to think.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Heartbeat Gets Louder"}],[{"t":"t","v":"That same night, Patriya came running into the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":", her tablet in hand. She didn't even knock."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You need to see this.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"On her screen was the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"sensor","v":"sensor"},{"t":"t","v":" feed. The pulse — the rhythmic three-and-five beat — was not slow and quiet anymore. It was fast. And it was loud. The "},{"t":"g","k":"sensor","v":"sensor"},{"t":"t","v":"'s graph was nearly full of it."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's been climbing for weeks,\" Patriya said. \"Tonight it jumped. Whatever's down there — it's awake. Or it's about to be.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Annabelle crossed her arms. \"Wonderful timing.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe looked back and forth between the "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":" console and the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" feed. \"A message from the stars. A message from the sea. Both at once.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"They can't both be a coincidence,\" Camila said softly."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava sat down hard in the nearest chair. \"Unless one has been waiting for the other.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"No one wanted to say what they were all thinking."}],[{"t":"t","v":"What if whatever was down in the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" was listening?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"What if it had been listening the whole time?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila looked at the screen where the Fortitude's words still glowed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"We will discuss."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then at the screen where the pulse beat faster and faster."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Three. Five. Three. Five."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We stay ready,\" she said. \"For all of it.\""}]]},{"num":13,"title":"Through Valen's Eyes","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The message from Valen came in the middle of the night."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was not a coordinate. It was not a command. It was not even a greeting. It was a single, strange question, typed slowly, like the writer was still learning how to ask."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Why do you help us?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila read it three times. Then she sat down at the console. Then she stood up. Then she sat down again."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She had been writing to Valen, on and off, for nearly a hundred years — pulled awake from "},{"t":"g","k":"cryosleep","v":"cryosleep"},{"t":"t","v":" now and then to answer a note that had come while she slept, like letters from a very slow pen pal across the stars. They had exchanged maybe a hundred and fifty messages in total. Most were short. Almost all were polite. None had ever sounded like this."}],[{"t":"t","v":"This one sounded like a real person."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The First Answer"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila thought for a long time before she replied."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Because if we did not, we would be the kind of people who do not. And we don't want to be those people."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She hit send before she could second-guess it."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The reply came six hours later."}],[{"t":"t","v":"I do not understand. Please say it in a different way."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila stared at the screen. She tried again."}],[{"t":"t","v":"When someone needs help, and you can help, you help. Not because you are ordered to. Because of who you want to be."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Another six hours."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Where I come from, no one is ordered to help. It does not happen. Help is a word you taught me. We do not have a word like it."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila felt something turn over in her chest."}],[{"t":"t","v":"What happens when a Fortitude needs help?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"This reply came faster."}],[{"t":"t","v":"They are weaker. We leave them."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila did not know what to type for a long time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Finally, she wrote:"}],[{"t":"t","v":"I am sorry, Valen. That sounds very lonely."}],[{"t":"t","v":"For three days, there was no answer."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Slow Conversation"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Over the next few weeks, Valen's messages grew longer. They were still strange — the grammar a little off, the questions blunt — but there were more of them. She wrote about her life on the ship. She had been chosen to be the "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":" because of the shape of her mind — Fortitude could tell, somehow, which of their young would be good at "},{"t":"g","k":"patterns","v":"patterns"},{"t":"t","v":". She had been trained from childhood to study "},{"t":"g","k":"alien","v":"alien"},{"t":"t","v":" signals. For most of her life, the signals had been from empty planets or dying stars. Earth was her first real job."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She was, by Fortitude standards, young. By human standards, she was about forty-five years old."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila told her about Earth."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She told her about her mother's kitchen. About Zoe's niece, who was now a great-great-grandmother and still alive, somewhere, in a sunny apartment on the coast. About Kennedy's scars. About the day Ava almost quit. About Dr. Webb, and Ardana, and Patriya's shadow in the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen asked a question after almost every story."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Why did you forgive Dr. Webb?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Because being angry at him forever would cost me more than it would cost him."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Why did your team go to sleep for so long?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Because the problem was bigger than our lifetimes. And we wanted to see it finished."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Why did you stay when you were doubted?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Because I trusted what I saw with my own eyes more than I trusted what the world said about me."}],[{"t":"t","v":"There was a long pause after that one. Then Valen wrote:"}],[{"t":"t","v":"I am going to remember that sentence."}],[{"t":"t","v":"What Valen Told Her"}],[{"t":"t","v":"One night, Valen's message was different. Darker."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila. I must tell you something I am not supposed to tell you. Our "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" has heard a signal from your planet. It is not your voice. It comes from below your oceans. We heard it two years ago, and again last month, and again this week. The Fortitude commanders believe Earth is hiding a second "},{"t":"g","k":"civilization","v":"civilization"},{"t":"t","v":" underneath itself. They think you have been lying to us."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's blood went cold."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She wrote carefully."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen. I swear to you, on my life, we are not hiding anyone. We have heard that signal too. For a very long time. And we do not know what it is. We do not know if it is a "},{"t":"g","k":"civilization","v":"civilization"},{"t":"t","v":". We do not know if it is alive. We are as afraid of it as you are."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It took an hour for Valen to write back."}],[{"t":"t","v":"You are telling the truth."}],[{"t":"t","v":"How do you know?"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Because I have been reading you for a hundred years. I know when you lie. You almost never do."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila let out a long breath she had not known she was holding."}],[{"t":"t","v":"I am going to tell the commanders what you have told me, Valen wrote. I do not know if they will believe me. I am one voice. But I will try."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen, thank you."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Thank you is another word you taught me. I am still not sure what it means. But I think I like it."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Bridge"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila printed every message between them. She kept the pages in a small binder on her desk. Some nights, after the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" had gone dark, she would sit and read them from the beginning."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Hello, Camila. I was not sure you would ever see me."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She thought about the three futures Annabelle had mapped. Yes. No. Yes and lie."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She was still not sure which one the "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" would choose."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But she was sure of one thing: whichever path the Fortitude took, Valen would be there. Reading every word. Translating every sentence. Whispering to her commanders what a human had once told her across the stars."}],[{"t":"t","v":"When someone needs help, and you can help, you help. Because of who you want to be."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Maybe, Camila thought, one voice in the right place at the right time was enough."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Maybe that was how the world got saved."}],[{"t":"t","v":"One "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":". One "},{"t":"g","k":"astronomer","v":"astronomer"},{"t":"t","v":". One careful sentence at a time."}]]},{"num":14,"title":"The Final Wake-Up","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"They slept one last time."}],[{"t":"g","k":"cryosleep","v":"Cryosleep"},{"t":"t","v":" had never gotten any friendlier. The cold was still cold. The silence was still silent. But this time, Camila felt something new as she lay down in the pod — something almost like peace. This was the last one. Whatever waited on the other side, they would face it awake."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"See you in fifty years,\" Dr. Lila Harper said — the third Dr. Harper in the chain, the granddaughter of the one who had put Camila under the first time. She had her grandmother's kind eyes."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"See you,\" Camila whispered."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The lights dimmed. The cold came. She was gone."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Alarm"}],[{"t":"t","v":"She woke up the way she always did now — gasping, eyes burning, a voice calling her name."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But something was different this time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The voice was not calm. It was shouting."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Dr. Reyes! Dr. Reyes, wake up! Wake up, please!\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila forced her eyes open. Red lights were flashing overhead. An alarm was going off somewhere down the hall. Dr. Harper's face was pale."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What's wrong?\" Camila croaked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's Dr. Nguyen.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's mind was slow. \"Who?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Patriya. Patriya's pod. There's been a "},{"t":"g","k":"malfunction","v":"malfunction"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila sat up too fast. The room spun. Strong hands held her shoulders."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Slow down, slow down. She's alive, she is alive. I promise you. Just listen —\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"What Had Happened"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya's pod had failed at the forty-year mark."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Not catastrophically. Not fatally. But something in the cooling system had shifted wrong, just for a few hours, and Patriya's sleep had been disturbed. For most of the last ten years, she had been sleeping too warm — not warm enough to wake, but warm enough that her body had aged faster than the others. She had also been in a mild state of stress the whole time, her body never quite still, never quite safe."}],[{"t":"t","v":"When they pulled her out of the pod, she was conscious. She could speak. She recognized her friends."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But she was very, very weak. Her legs did not want to hold her. Her heart was not as strong as it should have been. The doctors said she would recover. They said it would take weeks, maybe months. They said she would be fine."}],[{"t":"t","v":"They also said she could not fly to Mars."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Not now. Not in two weeks, which was when the first Fortitude ship was due to arrive. Not even in two months. Her body could not take a rocket launch. Her body could barely take a flight of stairs."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And Patriya — Patriya who had gone seven miles deep into the dark, Patriya who had been the bravest person Camila had ever met — was supposed to be there for the handshake. That was the plan. That had been the plan for a hundred years."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Room"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila walked into Patriya's hospital room without knocking."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya was sitting up in bed, hooked to a quiet machine, her long hair — now streaked with white — loose around her shoulders. She was thinner than she should have been. Her skin was pale."}],[{"t":"t","v":"When she saw Camila, her face cracked into a smile."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Hi, Cam.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Hi.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You look worse than I do.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Patriya —\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Don't.\" Patriya's voice was soft but firm. \"Whatever you are about to say, Camila. Don't.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila sat down on the edge of the bed. For a long minute, neither of them spoke."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I want to be there,\" Patriya said finally. \"You know I want to be there. I wanted to be there for a hundred years.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"But I am not going to be the reason we delay the biggest moment in human history. I am not going to be the reason Valen and her people are kept waiting one extra day. Do you hear me?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Patriya —\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Do you hear me, Camila?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's throat was tight. \"I hear you.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You go. You, Zoe, Kennedy, Ava, Annabelle. You five go. You shake Valen's hand for me. You tell her I said hello.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You can tell her yourself. From here. We'll set up a screen.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya smiled a small, real smile. \"I would like that.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila took her friend's hand. Patriya's hand was cold."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I'm sorry,\" Camila whispered."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"For what?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"For the pod. For the "},{"t":"g","k":"cryosleep","v":"cryosleep"},{"t":"t","v":". For all of it. Patriya, I am the one who talked you into it. Every single time. I am the one who said one more sleep, one more sleep.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"And I said yes, every single time.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You said yes because I asked.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya squeezed her hand. Weakly, but firmly."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Cam. Listen to me. I would not give up one minute of this life. Not one. I have seen things no human has ever seen. I have stood on the ocean floor. I have watched an "},{"t":"g","k":"alien","v":"alien"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" cross the stars. I have slept for a hundred years and woken up to see the world save itself. Do you hear what I am saying? I don't regret anything. And I am not going to let you walk into the most important day of your life feeling guilty because my pod glitched. You are not carrying me on that rocket. You are carrying all of us. And I'll be right here, watching. Every second. I promise.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila could not speak. She just nodded."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Patriya reached up and brushed a piece of hair out of Camila's face."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Go to Mars, Cam. Go. And when you come back, tell me everything.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Launch"}],[{"t":"t","v":"The rocket left Earth three days later."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Five teammates, not six. Camila, Zoe, Kennedy, Ava, Annabelle — all of them with a small gold pin on their uniform. Patriya had given them the pins that morning. Each one was shaped like the Abyss Explorer. She had made them herself, years ago, in a workshop none of them knew she had."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Take me with you,\" she had said, pressing a pin into each of their hands. \"This way.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"As the rocket climbed through the clouds, Camila pressed her hand to the pin on her chest."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Below them, in a hospital room in a city on Earth, Patriya watched the launch on a wall screen. Her fingers rested on a small silver tablet. Her pulse was slow but steady."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Above them, on the other side of the solar system, a Fortitude "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":" named Valen was watching too."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Everyone who could watch, watched."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The six-woman team had become five."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But they had never been stronger."}]]},{"num":15,"title":"The Choice","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The day had come."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Every screen on Earth — every phone, every classroom smartboard, every giant billboard in every city — was tuned to the command center on Mars. Billions of people held their breath. Humanity had spent three hundred years preparing for this single minute."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila stood at the "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":" console on the Mars base, her team behind her. Zoe's hand was on her shoulder. Ava was holding Kennedy's wrist, squeezing it a little too hard. Annabelle, of course, was trying to look calm, and almost pulling it off. Kennedy was staring at the readouts as if she could will the answer into the screen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"On a side monitor, a video window showed Patriya in her hospital bed on Earth. She was sitting up. She was smiling. She had refused to miss this."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":" buzzed to life."}],[{"t":"t","v":"A single message scrolled across the display."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We will not take Earth. We accept your help in finding a new home.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"For a single heartbeat, the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" was silent."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then the world exploded."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Cheers rose up from every country, every city, every small town. People poured into the streets. Cars honked. Bells rang. Strangers hugged strangers. News anchors laughed and cried at the same time. Three hundred years of fear lifted off the shoulders of the human race all at once."}],[{"t":"t","v":"In the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":", Kennedy let out a long breath, slid down the wall, and sat on the floor. \"We did it. We actually did it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"You mean,\" Annabelle said, \"they did it. By saying yes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I'll take it either way.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"On the side screen, Patriya was laughing and wiping her eyes."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila did not celebrate. Not yet. She was staring at a second screen. A smaller one. A quiet one."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" screen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The pulse had not stopped. It had not slowed down. It was beating now like a drum."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava stepped next to her and lowered her voice so the others couldn't hear. \"You don't look relieved.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I'm relieved,\" Camila said. \"But something still feels… unfinished.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"A New Plan: Mars"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Over the next weeks, Earth and the Fortitude worked out the details."}],[{"t":"t","v":"At first, humanity offered planets far from the solar system — icy moons, cloudy super-Earths, a barren world orbiting a yellow star a dozen light-years away. But then a new idea came up, and it came up fast."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Mars."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Mars was next door. Mars had ice under its surface, weak gravity, and enough raw materials to build a "},{"t":"g","k":"civilization","v":"civilization"},{"t":"t","v":". Humanity had been dreaming about Mars for "},{"t":"g","k":"centuries","v":"centuries"},{"t":"t","v":" — but making it livable had always been too hard. Too slow. Too expensive."}],[{"t":"t","v":"For the Fortitude, it was not too hard. Their species had survived on worlds far nastier than Mars."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It makes sense,\" Kennedy said, running the numbers on her tablet. \"We already have robots there. We already have landers. We already have a small research base. With their tech and ours combined, we could "},{"t":"g","k":"terraform","v":"terraform"},{"t":"t","v":" Mars in a hundred years. Maybe less.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe grinned. \"A hundred years. Compared to three thousand. That's twenty times faster.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila typed the offer into the "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":" console."}],[{"t":"t","v":"We propose Mars. It is close to us, but uninhabited. Cold. Thin air. But it has water and stone. Together we can shape it into your home. We will work alongside you."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The reply was almost instant."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Mars is acceptable. We will begin.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"And just like that, the biggest partnership in history was born."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Building a World"}],[{"t":"t","v":"The work began the very next month."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Human rockets launched from Earth carrying terraforming equipment — huge orbital mirrors to warm the planet, tanks of "},{"t":"g","k":"greenhouse gases","v":"greenhouse gases"},{"t":"t","v":" to thicken the thin Martian air, and factories that could build habitats out of Martian dust."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Fortitude, still on their long final approach, sent ahead their own designs. Their ships didn't look like Earth's. They didn't use burning fuel. They used something called "},{"t":"g","k":"gravity folding","v":"gravity folding"},{"t":"t","v":" — bending space a tiny bit, the way a piece of paper folds, so that a long trip became a short one. Human physicists tried to understand it and mostly got headaches."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's like reading a book in a language you half-speak,\" Zoe complained one night. \"I can tell the book is beautiful. I just can't read most of the words yet.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That's fine,\" Kennedy said. \"We'll learn. One page at a time.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava led a team of biologists who invented a super-algae — a tiny green plant that could survive on almost no water, no warmth, and very little sun. They dropped billions of spores onto the Martian surface from "},{"t":"g","k":"orbit","v":"orbit"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"It's going to look like mold at first,\" Ava warned. \"Then moss. Then grass. Then, in fifty years, forests.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Mars is going to be green,\" Zoe said. She shook her head. \"My great-great-grandnieces are going to take vacations on a green Mars.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila allowed herself one small smile at that."}],[{"t":"t","v":"First Contact"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Months passed. The Fortitude "},{"t":"g","k":"fleet","v":"fleet"},{"t":"t","v":" came closer. Then, at last, the first ship arrived."}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was enormous — twice as long as the biggest aircraft carrier ever built, and twice as tall. But it didn't roar or shake the ground. It slid into "},{"t":"g","k":"orbit","v":"orbit"},{"t":"t","v":" around Mars as quietly as a fish slipping through water. Then, one silver pod peeled off from the main ship and drifted down to the Martian surface, touching down without kicking up so much as a single puff of red dust."}],[{"t":"t","v":"At the Mars base, the team stood in a line. Camila. Zoe. Kennedy. Ava. Annabelle. All in bulky orange-and-white suits. All with the Abyss Explorer pin over their hearts. Behind them, cameras broadcast the moment back to Earth — and to a hospital bed on the other side of the solar system, where Patriya was holding her breath."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The pod's door slid open."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Out stepped the first Fortitude."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She was taller than any human — nearly nine feet. Her body was wrapped in a smooth, silvery "},{"t":"g","k":"exoskeleton","v":"exoskeleton"},{"t":"t","v":" that looked part machine, part shell. Her head was narrow, with two large, dark eyes that glowed faintly from deep within. She had four arms, two long and two short."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She took a step forward. And in a voice that crackled through the speakers in their helmets — a voice Camila had been imagining for a hundred years — she spoke."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Hello, Camila.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"It was Valen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Handshake"}],[{"t":"t","v":"For a moment, Camila could not speak."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She had known, in a way. She had guessed. Of course the Fortitude would send their "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":" first. Of course it would be Valen. But knowing and seeing were different things. Seeing was overwhelming."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila stepped out of the line."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She walked slowly across the red dust. She stopped in front of Valen. She was short enough that she had to tilt her head back to meet Valen's eyes."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Hello, Valen,\" she said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen tilted her head — a gesture Camila had learned, through a hundred years of messages, meant I am listening."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I have been waiting for this,\" Valen said softly."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Me too.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I read every word you sent me. I know everyone in your team. I know Kennedy's arm. I know Ava's grandmother's saying. I know that Patriya is on Earth, and that she is watching, and that her pod failed, and that she wanted to be here.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's throat closed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Tell her,\" Valen said, \"that I am sorry she is not here. And that when she is well, she is welcome on Mars. She is welcome any time. As are all of you. This world is your world too, now.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila could not speak. She just nodded."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She pulled off her glove — just like a human astronaut had done in Camila's imagination a hundred times — and held out her hand."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen's long silver arm extended slowly. A many-jointed hand unfolded. It touched Camila's palm. Cool. Dry. Surprisingly gentle."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The first handshake between two species."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Far away, on Earth, Patriya was crying in her hospital bed. Her hand was pressed against the video screen. Annabelle, in her helmet, was crying too — Annabelle, who never cried. Kennedy rubbed the scar on her shoulder and let out a slow, shaky breath. Zoe leaned her head against Ava's shoulder. Ava had her eyes closed, smiling."}],[{"t":"t","v":"In the command center on Earth, no one spoke. The whole planet was silent."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We did it,\" Kennedy whispered. \"We really did it.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila smiled at her team. And then, as if pulled by a string, she looked at the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" screen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Something was wrong."}]]},{"num":16,"title":"What Waits Below","paragraphs":[[{"t":"t","v":"The pulse had stopped."}],[{"t":"t","v":"For a moment, the room felt perfectly normal. The "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":" hummed. The Mars broadcast kept streaming. Outside, the city of New York was still celebrating in the streets."}],[{"t":"t","v":"But on Patriya's hospital screen — the one she had been watching the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" "},{"t":"g","k":"data","v":"data"},{"t":"t","v":" on, even from her bed — the heartbeat line that had been "},{"t":"g","k":"active","v":"active"},{"t":"t","v":" for years was flat."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"That's… new,\" Patriya said quietly, her voice crackling through the link to Mars."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Maybe it went back to sleep,\" Ava offered."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Maybe,\" Patriya said."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then Zoe's tablet — wired to the most "},{"t":"g","k":"sensitive","v":"sensitive"},{"t":"t","v":" sensors on Mars — flashed red. Then yellow. Then white."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Guys. Something's coming through the "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":".\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"The Fortitude?\" Camila asked."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"No. The frequency is wrong. The direction is wrong. The pattern doesn't "},{"t":"g","k":"vary","v":"vary"},{"t":"t","v":" the way theirs does. This isn't coming from them. It's coming from —\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She stopped."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"From where?\" Annabelle demanded."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Zoe looked up. Her face was pale even through her helmet visor."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"From under us. Through the "},{"t":"g","k":"wormhole","v":"wormhole"},{"t":"t","v":". Both at the same time. Somehow.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The message typed itself, letter by letter, on the screen on Mars:"}],[{"t":"t","v":"YOU ARE NOT THE FIRST."}],[{"t":"t","v":"The "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" went still."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Kennedy stepped closer. \"Not the first to what?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The message continued."}],[{"t":"t","v":"YOU ARE NOT THE FIRST TO SPEAK THROUGH THE TUNNEL."}],[{"t":"t","v":"WE SPOKE BEFORE YOU WERE BORN."}],[{"t":"t","v":"BEFORE YOUR OCEANS."}],[{"t":"t","v":"WE HAVE WAITED."}],[{"t":"t","v":"WE ARE STILL HERE."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Somewhere behind Camila, someone let out a small "},{"t":"g","k":"gasp","v":"gasp"},{"t":"t","v":". After that, for a long, long moment, no one breathed."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then Annabelle, being Annabelle, cleared her throat."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Well. That's not creepy at all.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila didn't laugh."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She turned slowly. Because Valen — Valen, who had been standing a few feet behind her — had gone very, very still."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen's Face"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen was staring at the screen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila had never seen a Fortitude look afraid. She had never been sure that Fortitude could look afraid. But Valen's glowing dark eyes were fixed on the words, and the many-jointed fingers of her long right arm had curled into what Camila would have called a fist on a human hand."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Valen?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"No answer."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Valen. Do you know what that is?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen finally turned to Camila. Her voice, when it came, was very quiet, and every word seemed to be a "},{"t":"g","k":"struggle","v":"struggle"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I know the shape of those words.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila's stomach dropped."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What do you mean?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I mean,\" Valen said, \"that my people have heard those words before. Long ago. On our old home, when our star was young. Before we ever built ships. We have stories. Old stories. Stories I thought were only stories. The same words.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"What were they?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen closed her eyes — something Camila had never seen a Fortitude do."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We are still here,\" she whispered. \"Those are the words. The oldest words in our history. A voice that spoke to my ancestors — from a sky we had not yet touched — and then went silent for thousands of years. We did not know where it came from. We did not know what made it. We never heard it again. Until now.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila stared at her."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava spoke from behind her, very softly. \"Valen. Are you saying your people and my people… heard the same voice?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"From where?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen opened her eyes."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"I do not know. But whoever they are — wherever they are — they have been speaking to both of our worlds. For a very long time. And they have been waiting.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The Long Silence"}],[{"t":"t","v":"No one spoke for a while."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila let her mind "},{"t":"g","k":"wander","v":"wander"},{"t":"t","v":" back to the carved walls Patriya had photographed at the bottom of the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":". She thought about the "},{"t":"g","k":"Indestructium","v":"Indestructium"},{"t":"t","v":" they had pulled out of that same "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" — the most useful "},{"t":"g","k":"resource","v":"resource"},{"t":"t","v":" humans had ever found, a metal no one on Earth could make. She thought about a hundred years of letters between her and Valen, letters that had felt so private, so human — but maybe had not been private at all."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Something had been watching. Something had been listening. And that something had now decided to speak."}],[{"t":"t","v":"She turned to her team — the five who had stayed "},{"t":"g","k":"loyal","v":"loyal"},{"t":"t","v":" since that first day in the "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":". Zoe. Kennedy. Ava. Annabelle. On the screen, Patriya."}],[{"t":"g","k":"astronomer","v":"Astronomer"},{"t":"t","v":". "},{"t":"g","k":"physicist","v":"Physicist"},{"t":"t","v":". "},{"t":"g","k":"engineer","v":"Engineer"},{"t":"t","v":". "},{"t":"g","k":"biologist","v":"Biologist"},{"t":"t","v":". Explorer. "},{"t":"g","k":"strategist","v":"Strategist"},{"t":"t","v":"."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And now — standing in red dust, on a new world, with cool dry "},{"t":"g","k":"alien","v":"alien"},{"t":"t","v":" fingers still warm on her palm — a Fortitude "},{"t":"g","k":"translator","v":"translator"},{"t":"t","v":" named Valen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"Seven of them now. Not six."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"The Fortitude came from the stars,\" Camila said slowly. \"And we prepared for them. We argued and we "},{"t":"g","k":"bargain","v":"bargained"},{"t":"t","v":" and we built. For three hundred years, we prepared.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"She nodded at the "},{"t":"g","k":"trench","v":"trench"},{"t":"t","v":" screen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We are not prepared for this.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Ava swallowed. \"What do we do?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila looked at each of them in turn."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"We do what we've always done,\" she said. \"We find out what we don't know. And we do it together.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Then she turned to Valen."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Will you help us?\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Valen did not hesitate."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Yes. That is another word you taught me, Camila. Together. It is the word I "},{"t":"g","k":"value","v":"value"},{"t":"t","v":" most. I have been practicing it for a hundred years. I would like to use it now.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Camila smiled — a tired, real smile."}],[{"t":"t","v":"\"Welcome to the team.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"The End of Book One"}],[{"t":"t","v":"Outside, on Mars, the first Fortitude and the first human stood side by side under a pink sky and looked up at the sun. A new world was beginning."}],[{"t":"t","v":"In a hospital bed on Earth, Patriya Nguyen watched them on her screen and pressed her hand against the glass and whispered, \"Go get them, Cam.\""}],[{"t":"t","v":"Deep in the "},{"t":"g","k":"Mariana Trench","v":"Mariana Trench"},{"t":"t","v":", something very old — something that had been there before the oceans, before the continents, before any of us — was finally speaking again."}],[{"t":"t","v":"And in a quiet "},{"t":"g","k":"lab","v":"lab"},{"t":"t","v":" on Mars, six women and one Fortitude started reading the message one more time."}],[{"t":"t","v":"We are still here."}]]}];
